    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nmini.git show line history buffer does not highlight all the diff in the buffer.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Use the below repro config in ``~/.config/repro/init.lua``.\n```lua\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim\"\nlocal clone_cmd = { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth=1\", \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\", mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\nvim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim\")\nrequire(\"mini.deps\").setup()\n\nrequire(\"mini.git\").setup()\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup()\n\nvim.o.number = true\nvim.o.wrap = false\nvim.cmd.colorscheme(\"minicyan\")\n\nMap = function(modes, suffix, rhs, desc, opts)\n\topts = opts or {}\n\tif not opts.silent then\n\t\topts.silent = true\n\tend\n\topts.desc = desc\n\tvim.keymap.set(modes, suffix, rhs, opts)\nend\nNmap = function(suffix, rhs, desc, opts)\n\tMap(\"n\", suffix, rhs, desc, opts)\nend\n\nNmap(\"ff\", \":Pick files<CR>\", \"Search files\")\nNmap(\"gC\", \":lua MiniGit.show_at_cursor()<CR>\", \"Git line history\")\n```\n2. Clone ``https://github.com/231tr0n/231tr0n.github.io.git``.\n3. Type ``NVIM_APPNAME=repro nvim`` in the cloned git repo git root.\n4. Open the file Codeeditor.svelte using the `ff` binding, which open file picker.\n5. Go to line number `137` and put the cursor on `f` in the word `fill`.\n6. Type `gC` binding to toggle line history.\n7. In the diff shown, type `G` to go to the bottom. You can see that the diff is not highlighted at the bottom. If you scroll from the bottom slowly to the top, you can see that the diff is half highlighted.",
