            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI both can not reproduce and pretty sure that this is not a 'mini.git' issue. All it does is sets a proper filetype (`git`) and delegates highlighting to how the user set up its highlighting. By default it uses built-in syntax highlighting which does behave like you describe: it can cut off before file end and stop computing highlighting further. This is for performance reasons. Try adjusting 'redrawtime' option or use `:syntax sync` (see `:h :syn-sync`).\n\nHere is the demo of how it looks for me:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8fd25113-5635-4ba1-9bd3-2ba5348606bc\n\nClosing as I am pretty sure it is not a 'mini.git' issue.",
